  m_Name: battle-pass
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: battle-pass
    Term: Battle Pass
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 8
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: A time-limited progression track that rewards play, often with
      a premium paid track.
    SimpleExplanation: A seasonal checklist of rewards you unlock by playing during
      the season.
    WhyItMatters: Battle passes monetize engagement while giving free players a clear
      goal ladder.
    Example: A ten-week pass grants cosmetics on free and premium tracks as XP accumulates.
    CommonMistake: Requiring impossible grind so premium buyers still cannot finish
      without more spend.
    PracticePrompt: Sketch a twenty-tier pass with earn rates that a median player
      can complete.
    GameUses:
    - Live seasons
    - Retention hooks
    - Cosmetic monetization
    RelatedTermIds:
    - metagame
    - live-ops
    - in-app-purchase
    - progression
    Tags:
    - monetization
    - seasons
    - progression
    Synonyms: []
